{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Want to skip to the implementation? Check out these Alpine examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/column-visibility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read your reactive inputs such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" through a getter (for example backing them with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alpine.reactive"},{"type":"text","value":") when creating the table, so the table sees updates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-visibility-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here's how you set up your table to use column visibility features. Adding the column visibility feature enables the related APIs."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n  createTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return local.data\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-visibility-alpine-guide","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility (Alpine) Guide"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The column visibility feature allows table columns to be hidden or shown dynamically. In v9, add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibilityFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" to your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" to enable this. There is a dedicated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" state and APIs for managing column visibility dynamically."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-visibility-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" state is a map of column IDs to boolean values. A column will be hidden if its ID is present in the map and the value is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":". If the column ID is not present in the map, or the value is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the column will be shown."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need to own the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" state yourself (for example, to persist user preferences), the recommended v9 approach is an external atom passed to the table's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"atoms"},{"type":"text","value":" option. External atoms give you fine-grained subscriptions anywhere in your app, and other code can read or write the visibility state without going through the component that owns the table. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/store"},{"type":"text","value":" is already a dependency of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/alpine-table"},{"type":"text","value":", so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAtom"},{"type":"text","value":" is available."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createAtom } from '@tanstack/store'\nimport {\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n  createTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\nimport type { ColumnVisibilityState } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nconst columnVisibilityAtom = createAtom<ColumnVisibilityState>({\n  columnId1: true,\n  columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n  columnId3: true,\n})\n\n// subscribe to the atom wherever you need the value\ncolumnVisibilityAtom.subscribe(() => {\n  // react to visibility changes\n})\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  //...\n  atoms: {\n    columnVisibility: columnVisibilityAtom,\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, the v8-style "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnVisibilityChange"},{"type":"text","value":" pattern is still supported by owning the slice in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alpine.reactive"},{"type":"text","value":". It can be convenient for simple integrations or when migrating v8 code, but it is less fine-grained than external atoms. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./table-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table State Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a deeper comparison."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const local = Alpine.reactive({\n  columnVisibility: {\n    columnId1: true,\n    columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n    columnId3: true,\n  } as ColumnVisibilityState,\n})\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  //...\n  state: {\n    get columnVisibility() {\n      return local.columnVisibility // connect the reactive slice back down to the table\n    },\n    //...\n  },\n  onColumnVisibilityChange: (updater) => {\n    local.columnVisibility =\n      typeof updater === 'function' ? updater(local.columnVisibility) : updater\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, if you don't need to manage the column visibility state outside of the table, you can still set the initial default column visibility state using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" is provided to both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" and a controlled option ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"atoms"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":"), the controlled value will take precedence and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" will be ignored. Only provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" in one place."}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  //...\n  initialState: {\n    columnVisibility: {\n      columnId1: true,\n      columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n      columnId3: true,\n    },\n    //...\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"disable-hiding-columns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disable Hiding Columns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, all columns can be hidden or shown. If you want to prevent certain columns from being hidden, you set the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableHiding"},{"type":"text","value":" column option to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" for those columns."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const columns = [\n  {\n    header: 'ID',\n    accessorKey: 'id',\n    enableHiding: false, // disable hiding for this column\n  },\n  {\n    header: 'Name',\n    accessorKey: 'name', // can be hidden\n  },\n]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-visibility-toggle-apis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility Toggle APIs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are several column API methods that are useful for rendering column visibility toggles in the UI."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getCanHide"},{"type":"text","value":" - Useful for disabling the visibility toggle for a column that has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableHiding"},{"type":"text","value":" set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsVisible"},{"type":"text","value":" - Useful for setting the initial state of the visibility toggle."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.toggleVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" - Useful for toggling the visibility of a column."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getToggleVisibilityHandler"},{"type":"text","value":" - Shortcut for hooking up the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.toggleVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" method to a UI event handler."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render a checkbox per column on real elements (not inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-html"},{"type":"text","value":"). Bind "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":checked"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsVisible()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":":disabled"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"!column.getCanHide()"},{"type":"text","value":", and call the handler returned by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getToggleVisibilityHandler"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@change"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<template x-for=\"column in table.getAllLeafColumns()\" :key=\"column.id\">\n  <label>\n    <input\n      type=\"checkbox\"\n      :checked=\"column.getIsVisible()\"\n      :disabled=\"!column.getCanHide()\"\n      @change=\"column.getToggleVisibilityHandler()($event)\"\n    />\n    <span x-text=\"column.id\"></span>\n  </label>\n</template>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A \"Toggle All\" checkbox can use the table-level helpers "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getIsAllColumnsVisible()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getToggleAllColumnsVisibilityHandler()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<label>\n  <input\n    type=\"checkbox\"\n    :checked=\"table.getIsAllColumnsVisible()\"\n    @change=\"table.getToggleAllColumnsVisibilityHandler()($event)\"\n  />\n  Toggle All\n</label>","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-visibility-aware-table-apis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility Aware Table APIs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you render your header, body, and footer cells, there are a lot of API options available. You may see APIs like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getAllLeafColumns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getAllCells"},{"type":"text","value":", but if you use these APIs, they will not take column visibility into account. Instead, you need to use the \"visible\" variants of these APIs, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getVisibleLeafColumns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getVisibleCells"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render cell and header content with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-html=\"FlexRender(...)\""},{"type":"text","value":", and use the visible-aware row models when iterating with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-for"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<table>\n  <thead>\n    <template\n      x-for=\"headerGroup in table.getHeaderGroups()\"\n      :key=\"headerGroup.id\"\n    >\n      <tr>\n        <!-- header groups already take column visibility into account -->\n        <template x-for=\"header in headerGroup.headers\" :key=\"header.id\">\n          <th :colspan=\"header.colSpan\">\n            <template x-if=\"!header.isPlaceholder\">\n              <span x-html=\"FlexRender({ header })\"></span>\n            </template>\n          </th>\n        </template>\n      </tr>\n    </template>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <template x-for=\"row in table.getRowModel().rows\" :key=\"row.id\">\n      <tr>\n        <!-- takes column visibility into account -->\n        <template x-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n          <td x-html=\"FlexRender({ cell })\"></td>\n        </template>\n      </tr>\n    </template>\n  </tbody>\n</table>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are using the Header Group APIs, they will already take column visibility into account."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"column-visibility-setup","text":"Column Visibility Setup","level":3},{"id":"column-visibility-alpine-guide","text":"Column Visibility (Alpine) Guide","level":2},{"id":"column-visibility-state","text":"Column Visibility State","level":3},{"id":"disable-hiding-columns","text":"Disable Hiding Columns","level":3},{"id":"column-visibility-toggle-apis","text":"Column Visibility Toggle APIs","level":3},{"id":"column-visibility-aware-table-apis","text":"Column Visibility Aware Table APIs","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these Alpine examples:\n\n- [Column Visibility](../examples/column-visibility)\n\nRead your reactive inputs such as `data` through a getter (for example backing them with `Alpine.reactive`) when creating the table, so the table sees updates.\n\n### Column Visibility Setup\n\nHere's how you set up your table to use column visibility features. Adding the column visibility feature enables the related APIs.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n  createTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return local.data\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Column Visibility (Alpine) Guide\n\nThe column visibility feature allows table columns to be hidden or shown dynamically. In v9, add `columnVisibilityFeature` to your `features` to enable this. There is a dedicated `columnVisibility` state and APIs for managing column visibility dynamically.\n\n### Column Visibility State\n\nThe `columnVisibility` state is a map of column IDs to boolean values. A column will be hidden if its ID is present in the map and the value is `false`. If the column ID is not present in the map, or the value is `true`, the column will be shown.\n\nIf you need to own the `columnVisibility` state yourself (for example, to persist user preferences), the recommended v9 approach is an external atom passed to the table's `atoms` option. External atoms give you fine-grained subscriptions anywhere in your app, and other code can read or write the visibility state without going through the component that owns the table. `@tanstack/store` is already a dependency of `@tanstack/alpine-table`, so `createAtom` is available.\n\n```ts\nimport { createAtom } from '@tanstack/store'\nimport {\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n  createTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\nimport type { ColumnVisibilityState } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nconst columnVisibilityAtom = createAtom<ColumnVisibilityState>({\n  columnId1: true,\n  columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n  columnId3: true,\n})\n\n// subscribe to the atom wherever you need the value\ncolumnVisibilityAtom.subscribe(() => {\n  // react to visibility changes\n})\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  //...\n  atoms: {\n    columnVisibility: columnVisibilityAtom,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nAlternatively, the v8-style `state.columnVisibility` plus `onColumnVisibilityChange` pattern is still supported by owning the slice in `Alpine.reactive`. It can be convenient for simple integrations or when migrating v8 code, but it is less fine-grained than external atoms. See the [Table State Guide](./table-state) for a deeper comparison.\n\n```ts\nconst local = Alpine.reactive({\n  columnVisibility: {\n    columnId1: true,\n    columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n    columnId3: true,\n  } as ColumnVisibilityState,\n})\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  //...\n  state: {\n    get columnVisibility() {\n      return local.columnVisibility // connect the reactive slice back down to the table\n    },\n    //...\n  },\n  onColumnVisibilityChange: (updater) => {\n    local.columnVisibility =\n      typeof updater === 'function' ? updater(local.columnVisibility) : updater\n  },\n})\n```\n\nAlternatively, if you don't need to manage the column visibility state outside of the table, you can still set the initial default column visibility state using the `initialState` option.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> If `columnVisibility` is provided to both `initialState` and a controlled option (`atoms` or `state`), the controlled value will take precedence and `initialState` will be ignored. Only provide `columnVisibility` in one place.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  //...\n  initialState: {\n    columnVisibility: {\n      columnId1: true,\n      columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n      columnId3: true,\n    },\n    //...\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Disable Hiding Columns\n\nBy default, all columns can be hidden or shown. If you want to prevent certain columns from being hidden, you set the `enableHiding` column option to `false` for those columns.\n\n```ts\nconst columns = [\n  {\n    header: 'ID',\n    accessorKey: 'id',\n    enableHiding: false, // disable hiding for this column\n  },\n  {\n    header: 'Name',\n    accessorKey: 'name', // can be hidden\n  },\n]\n```\n\n### Column Visibility Toggle APIs\n\nThere are several column API methods that are useful for rendering column visibility toggles in the UI.\n\n- `column.getCanHide` - Useful for disabling the visibility toggle for a column that has `enableHiding` set to `false`.\n- `column.getIsVisible` - Useful for setting the initial state of the visibility toggle.\n- `column.toggleVisibility` - Useful for toggling the visibility of a column.\n- `column.getToggleVisibilityHandler` - Shortcut for hooking up the `column.toggleVisibility` method to a UI event handler.\n\nRender a checkbox per column on real elements (not inside `x-html`). Bind `:checked` to `column.getIsVisible()`, `:disabled` to `!column.getCanHide()`, and call the handler returned by `getToggleVisibilityHandler` from `@change`.\n\n```html\n<template x-for=\"column in table.getAllLeafColumns()\" :key=\"column.id\">\n  <label>\n    <input\n      type=\"checkbox\"\n      :checked=\"column.getIsVisible()\"\n      :disabled=\"!column.getCanHide()\"\n      @change=\"column.getToggleVisibilityHandler()($event)\"\n    />\n    <span x-text=\"column.id\"></span>\n  </label>\n</template>\n```\n\nA \"Toggle All\" checkbox can use the table-level helpers `table.getIsAllColumnsVisible()` and `table.getToggleAllColumnsVisibilityHandler()`.\n\n```html\n<label>\n  <input\n    type=\"checkbox\"\n    :checked=\"table.getIsAllColumnsVisible()\"\n    @change=\"table.getToggleAllColumnsVisibilityHandler()($event)\"\n  />\n  Toggle All\n</label>\n```\n\n### Column Visibility Aware Table APIs\n\nWhen you render your header, body, and footer cells, there are a lot of API options available. You may see APIs like `table.getAllLeafColumns` and `row.getAllCells`, but if you use these APIs, they will not take column visibility into account. Instead, you need to use the \"visible\" variants of these APIs, such as `table.getVisibleLeafColumns` and `row.getVisibleCells`.\n\nRender cell and header content with `x-html=\"FlexRender(...)\"`, and use the visible-aware row models when iterating with `x-for`:\n\n```html\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <template\n      x-for=\"headerGroup in table.getHeaderGroups()\"\n      :key=\"headerGroup.id\"\n    >\n      <tr>\n        <!-- header groups already take column visibility into account -->\n        <template x-for=\"header in headerGroup.headers\" :key=\"header.id\">\n          <th :colspan=\"header.colSpan\">\n            <template x-if=\"!header.isPlaceholder\">\n              <span x-html=\"FlexRender({ header })\"></span>\n            </template>\n          </th>\n        </template>\n      </tr>\n    </template>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <template x-for=\"row in table.getRowModel().rows\" :key=\"row.id\">\n      <tr>\n        <!-- takes column visibility into account -->\n        <template x-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n          <td x-html=\"FlexRender({ cell })\"></td>\n        </template>\n      </tr>\n    </template>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n\nIf you are using the Header Group APIs, they will already take column visibility into account.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Column Visibility (Alpine) Guide\n---\n\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these Alpine examples:\n\n- [Column Visibility](../examples/column-visibility)\n\nRead your reactive inputs such as `data` through a getter (for example backing them with `Alpine.reactive`) when creating the table, so the table sees updates.\n\n### Column Visibility Setup\n\nHere's how you set up your table to use column visibility features. Adding the column visibility feature enables the related APIs.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n  createTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return local.data\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Column Visibility (Alpine) Guide\n\nThe column visibility feature allows table columns to be hidden or shown dynamically. In v9, add `columnVisibilityFeature` to your `features` to enable this. There is a dedicated `columnVisibility` state and APIs for managing column visibility dynamically.\n\n### Column Visibility State\n\nThe `columnVisibility` state is a map of column IDs to boolean values. A column will be hidden if its ID is present in the map and the value is `false`. If the column ID is not present in the map, or the value is `true`, the column will be shown.\n\nIf you need to own the `columnVisibility` state yourself (for example, to persist user preferences), the recommended v9 approach is an external atom passed to the table's `atoms` option. External atoms give you fine-grained subscriptions anywhere in your app, and other code can read or write the visibility state without going through the component that owns the table. `@tanstack/store` is already a dependency of `@tanstack/alpine-table`, so `createAtom` is available.\n\n```ts\nimport { createAtom } from '@tanstack/store'\nimport {\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n  createTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\nimport type { ColumnVisibilityState } from '@tanstack/alpine-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nconst columnVisibilityAtom = createAtom<ColumnVisibilityState>({\n  columnId1: true,\n  columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n  columnId3: true,\n})\n\n// subscribe to the atom wherever you need the value\ncolumnVisibilityAtom.subscribe(() => {\n  // react to visibility changes\n})\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  //...\n  atoms: {\n    columnVisibility: columnVisibilityAtom,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nAlternatively, the v8-style `state.columnVisibility` plus `onColumnVisibilityChange` pattern is still supported by owning the slice in `Alpine.reactive`. It can be convenient for simple integrations or when migrating v8 code, but it is less fine-grained than external atoms. See the [Table State Guide](./table-state) for a deeper comparison.\n\n```ts\nconst local = Alpine.reactive({\n  columnVisibility: {\n    columnId1: true,\n    columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n    columnId3: true,\n  } as ColumnVisibilityState,\n})\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  //...\n  state: {\n    get columnVisibility() {\n      return local.columnVisibility // connect the reactive slice back down to the table\n    },\n    //...\n  },\n  onColumnVisibilityChange: (updater) => {\n    local.columnVisibility =\n      typeof updater === 'function' ? updater(local.columnVisibility) : updater\n  },\n})\n```\n\nAlternatively, if you don't need to manage the column visibility state outside of the table, you can still set the initial default column visibility state using the `initialState` option.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> If `columnVisibility` is provided to both `initialState` and a controlled option (`atoms` or `state`), the controlled value will take precedence and `initialState` will be ignored. Only provide `columnVisibility` in one place.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nconst table = createTable({\n  features,\n  //...\n  initialState: {\n    columnVisibility: {\n      columnId1: true,\n      columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n      columnId3: true,\n    },\n    //...\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Disable Hiding Columns\n\nBy default, all columns can be hidden or shown. If you want to prevent certain columns from being hidden, you set the `enableHiding` column option to `false` for those columns.\n\n```ts\nconst columns = [\n  {\n    header: 'ID',\n    accessorKey: 'id',\n    enableHiding: false, // disable hiding for this column\n  },\n  {\n    header: 'Name',\n    accessorKey: 'name', // can be hidden\n  },\n]\n```\n\n### Column Visibility Toggle APIs\n\nThere are several column API methods that are useful for rendering column visibility toggles in the UI.\n\n- `column.getCanHide` - Useful for disabling the visibility toggle for a column that has `enableHiding` set to `false`.\n- `column.getIsVisible` - Useful for setting the initial state of the visibility toggle.\n- `column.toggleVisibility` - Useful for toggling the visibility of a column.\n- `column.getToggleVisibilityHandler` - Shortcut for hooking up the `column.toggleVisibility` method to a UI event handler.\n\nRender a checkbox per column on real elements (not inside `x-html`). Bind `:checked` to `column.getIsVisible()`, `:disabled` to `!column.getCanHide()`, and call the handler returned by `getToggleVisibilityHandler` from `@change`.\n\n```html\n<template x-for=\"column in table.getAllLeafColumns()\" :key=\"column.id\">\n  <label>\n    <input\n      type=\"checkbox\"\n      :checked=\"column.getIsVisible()\"\n      :disabled=\"!column.getCanHide()\"\n      @change=\"column.getToggleVisibilityHandler()($event)\"\n    />\n    <span x-text=\"column.id\"></span>\n  </label>\n</template>\n```\n\nA \"Toggle All\" checkbox can use the table-level helpers `table.getIsAllColumnsVisible()` and `table.getToggleAllColumnsVisibilityHandler()`.\n\n```html\n<label>\n  <input\n    type=\"checkbox\"\n    :checked=\"table.getIsAllColumnsVisible()\"\n    @change=\"table.getToggleAllColumnsVisibilityHandler()($event)\"\n  />\n  Toggle All\n</label>\n```\n\n### Column Visibility Aware Table APIs\n\nWhen you render your header, body, and footer cells, there are a lot of API options available. You may see APIs like `table.getAllLeafColumns` and `row.getAllCells`, but if you use these APIs, they will not take column visibility into account. Instead, you need to use the \"visible\" variants of these APIs, such as `table.getVisibleLeafColumns` and `row.getVisibleCells`.\n\nRender cell and header content with `x-html=\"FlexRender(...)\"`, and use the visible-aware row models when iterating with `x-for`:\n\n```html\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <template\n      x-for=\"headerGroup in table.getHeaderGroups()\"\n      :key=\"headerGroup.id\"\n    >\n      <tr>\n        <!-- header groups already take column visibility into account -->\n        <template x-for=\"header in headerGroup.headers\" :key=\"header.id\">\n          <th :colspan=\"header.colSpan\">\n            <template x-if=\"!header.isPlaceholder\">\n              <span x-html=\"FlexRender({ header })\"></span>\n            </template>\n          </th>\n        </template>\n      </tr>\n    </template>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <template x-for=\"row in table.getRowModel().rows\" :key=\"row.id\">\n      <tr>\n        <!-- takes column visibility into account -->\n        <template x-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n          <td x-html=\"FlexRender({ cell })\"></td>\n        </template>\n      </tr>\n    </template>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n\nIf you are using the Header Group APIs, they will already take column visibility into account.\n"}
